  "Movies_and_TV:protocol": "Versioned rules printed before effects; only diagnostic corruption pools use training transition counts. No auxiliary recommendation scores or model fitting.",
  "Movies_and_TV:coverage": "Actual users, unique prefixes, plans and failures. Failed matching removes the entire four-plan block; absence is not zero effect. Doses can have different support.",
  "Movies_and_TV:architecture": "Possible offsets include causal-summary gates when supplied implementation is recognized. Unknown architecture disables structural interpretation. Masks may reduce possible reachability. Structural reachability is not learned influence; exact path counts unavailable.",
  "Movies_and_TV:chunked_rank_synthetic_check": "Chunked score/rank tie counter verified against exhaustive synthetic sorting at several chunk sizes.",
  "Movies_and_TV:identity_controls": "Repeated identical-input catalog score discrepancy and target-rank change; expected zero within numerical precision. Causality, all-padding and applicable unreachable checks are in architecture. These local controls do not prove calibration or CI coverage.",
  "Movies_and_TV:matching_failures": "Auditable user/cut/dose/draw failures and pool sizes. A failed greedy assignment is an algorithmic failure, not proof that no valid assignment exists. No tolerance is relaxed; effects condition on successful assignments.",
  "Movies_and_TV:sampler_designs": "Per-prefix deterministic sampler seed, actual module-source hashes, support and recognition status. Recognized supplied sampler is uniform without replacement on IDs outside the complete training history. Prefix inputs still contain only earlier interactions. Each 64-negative diagnostic draw has pi=min(64,N)/N on its actual support and zero elsewhere; no eligibility renormalization. First min(training_negative_count,N) entries reproduce the training accepted-set distribution when its count is at most 64. Unrecognized implementations receive diagnostic-only sampling claims. Hashes identify inspected sources, not a proof for arbitrary modified implementations.",
  "Movies_and_TV:historical_negative_exposure": "Unavailable without actual training context-negative logs; post-training diagnostic draws cannot reconstruct historical exposure or contemporaneous gradients.",
  "Movies_and_TV:gradient_reference_comparison": "Optional autograd comparison omitted under the fixed probe-work cap. Reported objective logit derivatives are analytical per-position derivatives, not parameter-gradient alignment, logical-batch gradients or historical optimizer contributions.",
  "Movies_and_TV:outranker_transitions": "Raw successful plan counts by variant for zero-to-zero, zero-to-positive, positive-to-zero and positive-to-positive strict-outranker transitions. Missing keys mean no observed transition of that type. Rank/count differences retain zero-outranker cases; coverage differences require nonempty outranker sets in both contexts.",
  "Movies_and_TV:audit_support": "Eligible and retained distinct prefixes/users per variant plus history-length and training-target-frequency counts. Retained strata deduplicate prefixes across corruption draws; eligible strata count all clean prefixes. Effects condition on successful complete cases and metric-specific observed_users in intervention_effects; no population weighting is applied.",
  "Movies_and_TV:competitor_audit": "Stored in baseline and paired observations. E excludes target/PAD and freezes original-full-prefix eligibility; restricted contexts remove the same inserted IDs. H uses strict score outranking; ties and lower-ID ties are separate. C_count is unique sampled H coverage; C0 is its exact design expectation; their ratio is null for empty H or zero C0. C_soft is unique sampled exp-score mass divided by eligible-negative mass. p_target uses target plus E; A=(1-p_target)*C_soft; M=p_target+A. Empty sampled sets have zero captured mass; empty E makes C_soft undefined. Stable logsumexp uses raw temperature-one logits. 2*(1-M) is the full-versus-unique-subset softmax logit-gradient L1 identity only, without sampling corrections, multiplicity weighting or batch coefficients. Analytical negative and positive gradients use the recognized actual objective and its training draw count, before supervised-position batch averaging/clipping; restricted losses are diagnostic extensions. Repetition records preserve accepted IDs, retained unique IDs, multiplicities, exclusions and denominators. Paired sampler SE and quantiles describe shared-draw differences conditional on each fixed corruption, separate from the corruption_mc_se and user-bootstrap intervals. Inner draws are averaged before prefix/user aggregation and never count as users. Context-independent coverage baselines measure accessibility, not optimization quality.",
  "Movies_and_TV:embedding_collapse_score": "Sampled mean pairwise item cosine mapped to [0,1]. Near 0.5 means mean cosine near zero; alignment alone cannot establish collapse or recommendation quality.",
  "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_mean": "Mean positive-minus-negative logit over valid aligned training-loader positions; in-sample sampled separation only.",
  "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_p10": "Empirical lower tenth percentile of valid training-loader margins; null if unavailable.",
  "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": "Fraction of valid training positions where negative score exceeds positive score.",
  "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": "Fraction of valid training positions with margin below protocol eps.",
  "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown": "Low/wrong-margin counts; category lists empty because item categories are unavailable.",
  "Movies_and_TV:training_prefix_hr10_user_mean": "Training-target exact eligible-catalog HR@10 averaged within user then across users; not host validation or generalization.",
  "Movies_and_TV:intervention_effects": "Changed-minus-clean ranks, HR@10, target score and fixed-negative mean margin; positive delta_rank is worse. Overlap is top-10 intersection/original top-10 size. Draws average within prefix, prefixes within user, then users equally. CI95 is exploratory percentile bootstrap of user means, null below two users. corruption_mc_se separately propagates within-prefix draw variance, conditional on successful matching and treating prefix draws as independent; null when any contributing prefix has fewer than two observations. More draws do not add independent users. recent_minus_older is a paired difference on the same successful four-plan blocks, with the same restricted catalog; never assume monotonic dose response.",
  "Movies_and_TV:strata": "Fixed prefix, training-frequency, repeated-target, transition, reachability and displacement strata. Displacement bins are [0,.5), [.5,1), [1,infinity); displacement is measured, not matched. Compare bands only where both have support; intervals are exploratory without multiplicity or coverage guarantees.",
